        "id": 221502,
        "name": "The Mariner",
        "username": "The_Mariner",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/the_mariner/{size}/2025_2.png",
        "created_at": "2018-08-18T15:23:45.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>While there aren’t any strict team bonuses in Sentinels, teams are designed to work better (or worse, as appropriate) together. &nbsp;If you’ve played with the Prime Wardens variants, for instance, you’ve probably bounced more plays and powers around than you can count. &nbsp;It almost feels like you’ve mashed five superheroes together into a larger, more merchandisable supersuperhero. &nbsp;The Freedom Five sort of feel the same way. &nbsp;There are other, “unofficial” teams that work well together, both thematically and mechanically: try F6 Unity, Benchmark, Omnitron-U, and FS Parse, or Stuntman, Mr. Fixer, Expatriette, and Guise (the best- and grittiest- hero).</p>",
        "post_number": 2,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:54:11.848Z",
